  "description": "BugWars is a high-energy coding challenge focused on debugging , problem - solving , and programming skills. Participants will tackle a range of coding problems designed to test their ability to identify errors, analyze logic, optimize solutions, and think under pressure. Covering concepts from DSA and Competitive Programming , the event challenges participants to turn broken code into efficient, working solutions. Participation is individual-only, making it a fair and thrilling competition for all coders and debuggers What we're looking for: Problem Solving : Strong logical and analytical thinking Debugging Skills : Identifying and fixing errors efficiently DSA & CP : Familiarity with core concepts and algorithms Code Optimization : Improving solutions for efficiency and performance Attention to Detail : Spotting logical, syntactical, and runtime errors Competitive Mindset : Ability to solve problems under time constraints Rules: Solo participation The contest will last for 2 hours There will be 3 winners in the contest The exact format and the platforms will be revealed then and there Participants must strictly avoid cheating, plagiarism, or using AI tools/assistants — violations will lead to immediate disqualification. Goodies, prizes, and certificates will be awarded to winners of each mini game. Participation Certificates will be awarded to all participants",
